==Battleground==
*Infinite [[UltraBaaBaa]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Diabrollow]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*6 [[Darkmadillo]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*8 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Youcan]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Wicked Face]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is a pretty boring [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] stage with up to six Darkmadillos, meaning you really need to watch out for them stacking. They can easily be taken care of with assistance from [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], which you should have in your lineup anyways for dealing with UltraBaaBaa and Diabrollow respectively. The main issue with this stage is the two Youcans that spawn about 70 seconds apart from each other. While the first Youcan dies to [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], the second one will be much more annoying given the lack of room. Because of this, after you kill the first Youcan, try and push the Wicked Face back to the enemy base while chipping him with Supercar and [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]. Given Wicked Face's slow attack rate and light peons, it should be easy for you to land Supercar hits even if you normally struggle with timing. Once the second Youcan appears, break his [[Barrier]], then kill him with a bunch of Royal Guards and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]. After both Youcans are dead, clean up Wicked Face and you are free to win.

==Trivia==
*The "Dreams" in Dreams and Illusions could be a reference to [[Youcan]], as his Japanese name (大夢くん ''Ōmu-kun'') contains the kanji for dream (夢) and his Japanese description says his parents gave him this name because they wanted him to have a big dream about his future.

